# Line endings for everything that runs on a Linux VM.
#
# install.sh curls each file from GitHub raw, so what a VM executes is the
# stored blob. A shell script stored with CRLF has a shebang ending in \r, and
# Linux reports "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — naming an
# interpreter that plainly exists, which is among the least helpful errors it
# is possible to ship.
#
# The path rules used to be depth-shaped: `corekit/*/*` matched exactly two
# levels. The platform/ move put the daemon launchers at platform/runtime/ and
# every one of them silently fell out of coverage. Depth is not a category, and
# these rules now name the trees.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

platform/**     text eol=lf
corekit/**      text eol=lf
skills/**       text eol=lf
infra/**        text eol=lf
bin/**          text eol=lf

# Role bundles ship as content, not code, and are hashed. A CRLF SOUL_APPEND.md
# is a different content digest from the same file, so an agent would resync on
# every apply and never converge. Organ firmware now lives under platform/,
# which is covered above.
specialties/**  text eol=lf
operator/**     text eol=lf

# Some guides ship to VMs as skill reference material.
docs/**  text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf

infra/manifests/*.txt text eol=lf
install.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these, and never let a text rule above claim them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
